---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---
<Layout title="Privacy Policy on ValoArt" description="ValoArt Privacy Policy. What data we collect, what we do not collect, and how analytics and copy counts work." active="">
  <div class="page-header">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p>Last updated: 23 October 2026</p>
  </div>

  <section class="legal">
    <p>
      ValoArt is a fan-made website for Valorant chat ASCII art. You can browse
      arts, generate banners, and paint on a canvas without creating an account.
      This policy explains, in plain language, what we collect and what we do not.
    </p>

    <h2>What we do not collect</h2>
    <p>
      We do not require an account, an email address, or a login to use ValoArt.
      We do not ask for your name, address, or payment details, and we do not
      sell personal data to anyone.
    </p>

    <h2>What we do collect</h2>
    <h3>Analytics</h3>
    <p>
      We use Rybbit analytics (hosted at stats.zruvix.com) to understand which
      pages are visited and how the site is used, so we can improve it. Rybbit
      is designed to be privacy-friendly and does not require an account from
      visitors. Analytics data is aggregated and is not used to identify you
      personally.
    </p>
    <h3>Copy counts</h3>
    <p>
      When you copy an art, a banner, or a canvas design, we increment a single
      global counter for that item (for example, “art-1: 1 copy”). This counter
      is stored in a database and is shared by all visitors. It is not tied to
      you, your device, or your account. It only records that a copy happened,
      not who copied it.
    </p>
    <h3>Local storage in your browser</h3>
    <p>
      Some features store data only in your own browser, not on our servers:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Canvas arts you publish are saved in your browser's session storage so
        they can be shown at the top of the Arts page during that session.
      </li>
      <li>
        If our copy-count service is unreachable, a fallback copy count may be
        kept in your browser's local storage. It is never added to the global
        total.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Clearing your browser's site data will remove these local items. They are
      not sent to us except as described above.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies</h2>
    <p>
      ValoArt itself does not set advertising cookies. Analytics and hosting
      services may use cookies or similar storage to count visits and keep the
      site working. You can block cookies in your browser settings; the site
      will still work for browsing and copying arts, although some counts may
      not be recorded.
    </p>

    <h2>Third-party services</h2>
    <p>
      ValoArt is hosted on Vercel, uses Rybbit for analytics, and uses a Neon
      Postgres database for global copy counts. Those services process data only
      as described above and under their own privacy policies. ValoArt does not
      control their internal data handling beyond the settings we use.
    </p>

    <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
    <p>
      ValoArt is not directed at children under 13, and we do not knowingly
      collect personal data from children. If you believe a child has provided
      personal data to us, please contact us and we will remove it.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this policy from time to time. The “Last updated” date at
      the top will change when we do, and continued use of the site after a
      change means you accept the updated policy.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      If you have questions about this policy, or you own an art in the gallery
      and would like it removed, please open an issue on the ValoArt GitHub
      repository at github.com/muse-codez/valoart, or contact us via ruvix.lol.
    </p>

    <h2>Disclaimer</h2>
    <p>
      ValoArt is a fan project and is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or
      connected to Riot Games, Inc. VALORANT is a trademark of Riot Games, Inc.
    </p>
  </section>

  <style>
    .legal { padding: 0 0 80px; max-width: 760px; }
    .legal h2 {
      font-family: 'Outfit', system-ui, sans-serif;
      font-weight: 700;
      font-size: 24px;
      margin: 32px 0 10px;
    }
    .legal h3 {
      font-family: 'Outfit', system-ui, sans-serif;
      font-weight: 600;
      font-size: 18px;
      margin: 20px 0 8px;
    }
    .legal p, .legal li {
      font-family: 'Figtree', system-ui, sans-serif;
      color: #d8dde2;
      line-height: 1.7;
      margin: 0 0 12px;
    }
    .legal ul { padding-left: 20px; }
  </style>
</Layout>
